SUMMARY:IMPROMPTU: CoffeeTue- HS Mollys Courtyard Cafe (23R) -- RSVP requi
 red
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nRide Leader: Barry David\
 nRide Sweep: open\n\nCoffeeTue rides:\n• A rotating start location\, not
  a school\n• A predetermined route\n• 25+/- mile routes\n• 12 to 14 
 and 14 to 16 mph average pace\n• Usually no sweep\n• “short” stop 
 for refreshment/coffee mid-route at [Molly's Courtyard Cafe](https://www.m
 ollyscourtyardcafe.com/)\n\nLike an All Class Ride\, CoffeeTue does not ha
 ve a single pace.\nThere will be multiple regroup points during the ride.\
 nThe CoffeeTue rides are social rides\, but cyclists are not expected to s
 tay in one group. Cyclists may pedal at their own comfortable paces. A pla
 nned stop to regroup is recommended. *Please be supportive of the other cy
 clists to avoid anyone biking alone or being dropped off the back of the l
 ast group.*\n**Be Safe\, Have Fun\, and Ride Together**\n\nClick for [Ride
  with GPS](https://routes.lancasterbikeclub.net/cue/hs-mollys-courtyard-ca
 fe-23r/)\n\nHelmets are mandatory. No ear buds. Please bring water and a b
 asic repair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump/CO2 inflator).\n\nTo elim
 inate passing around a pen and paper waiver\, we require LBC Club membersh
 ip and Meetup RSVP below to join this ride.\n\nBeing on Meetup does not me
 an you are a club member. [Join here](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/co
 ntent.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148).\n\nYour RSVP is your agreement to a
 bide by the club's [Code of Conduct](https://lancbikeclub.clubexpress.com/
 content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=323984) \,\n[Rules of the
  Road](https://lancbikeclub.clubexpress.com/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_i
 d=257148&module_id=325159) \, and [Ride Waiver](https://lancasterbikeclub.
 net/docs.ashx?id=454318)
